.TH git-state "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset 0.156.0" "SMI Git Command"
.SH NAME
git-state \- show the branches and the working tree status of a Git repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git state
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBgit state\fR command shows the local branches, the current one marked, and then the status of the
working tree, the same as \fBgit branch\fR followed by \fBgit status\fR.
.PP
Git runs it as a subcommand because the executable \fBgit-state\fR is in the \fBPATH\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B git state
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
